WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.227 --> 00:00:02.967
- I'm not gonna lie, I'm
gettin' a little nervous!

00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:03.909
- This is my nightmare.

00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:05.314
(Fatima and Brian laughing)

00:00:05.314 --> 00:00:07.385
(intense music)

00:00:07.385 --> 00:00:09.468
- We have an injury here!

00:00:10.645 --> 00:00:13.978
(energetic dance music)

00:00:16.222 --> 00:00:18.143
Wow, there's so many
beautiful people everywhere.

00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:20.941
Okay, so this week,
we're in Miami, Florida!

00:00:20.941 --> 00:00:21.850
I'm on my way to Juvia,

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:24.026
one of the best
restaurants in South Beach!

00:00:24.026 --> 00:00:25.486
But first, let's make a quick stop,

00:00:25.486 --> 00:00:29.069
to pick up Chef Sunny
Oh, in the 2017 RAV4!

00:00:31.045 --> 00:00:32.452
Hey, what's up, Chef Sunny?

00:00:32.452 --> 00:00:33.510
- What's goin' on?

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:34.343
- How ya doin'?

00:00:34.343 --> 00:00:35.198
- I'm good, how are you?

00:00:35.198 --> 00:00:36.303
- I'm doing good.

00:00:36.303 --> 00:00:37.331
Nice to finally meet you!

00:00:37.331 --> 00:00:38.259
- It's nice to meet you, too.

00:00:38.259 --> 00:00:39.740
- Tell me a little bit about yourself.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.589
- I was originally born in Korea.

00:00:41.589 --> 00:00:44.442
Korean food is, without a
doubt, one of my favorite foods.

00:00:44.442 --> 00:00:46.500
I remember watching my
mother, singing and cooking,

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.408
when I was a kid.

00:00:47.408 --> 00:00:49.112
And she had great knife skills.

00:00:49.112 --> 00:00:51.947
- Singing, cooking,
and great knife skills.

00:00:51.947 --> 00:00:53.561
That's quite the triple threat.

00:00:53.561 --> 00:00:54.989
Can you tell us a little bit about Juvia?

00:00:54.989 --> 00:00:56.560
- [Sunny] Juvia has been
around for about five years,

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.475
bringing together a union of French ideas,

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:02.855
as well as Japanese,
and Peruvian influences.

00:01:02.855 --> 00:01:05.374
- [Carl] What do we have in
store for our couples today?

00:01:05.374 --> 00:01:07.236
- [Sunny] We have local black grouper.

00:01:07.236 --> 00:01:09.888
Couples are gonna have fun
with some knife techniques,

00:01:09.888 --> 00:01:13.638
and it should be light, and healthy.

00:01:13.638 --> 00:01:16.638
(piano party music)

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:19.628
- [Carl] Hello, everyone.

00:01:19.628 --> 00:01:21.500
My name is Carl Monroe,
and I am your host.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.158
Welcome to Tasty Date Night!

00:01:23.158 --> 00:01:26.246
(crowd cheering)

00:01:26.246 --> 00:01:27.268
Today, we're here, in South Beach,

00:01:27.268 --> 00:01:29.549
to watch as two couples
put their relationship,

00:01:29.549 --> 00:01:31.941
and culinary skills,
through the ultimate test,

00:01:31.941 --> 00:01:33.038
in a cooking showdown.

00:01:33.038 --> 00:01:34.430
Whoever impresses our judge the most,

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:36.956
can look forward to a
romantic date night out,

00:01:36.956 --> 00:01:37.885
here, at Juvia.

00:01:37.885 --> 00:01:40.477
(crowd cheering)

00:01:40.477 --> 00:01:42.976
Our first couple have been
together for 17 years!

00:01:42.976 --> 00:01:45.344
Please, help me welcome, Brian and Fatima!

00:01:45.344 --> 00:01:47.785
(crowd cheering)

00:01:47.785 --> 00:01:49.138
- We love all different kinds of foods.

00:01:49.138 --> 00:01:51.129
So, then, we like to
experiment with new recipes

00:01:51.129 --> 00:01:51.962
all the time.

00:01:51.962 --> 00:01:52.795
- And I'm Spanish, and Cuban,

00:01:52.795 --> 00:01:56.269
so I like to bring in a little
extra mix, a little flair!

00:01:56.269 --> 00:01:58.028
- A lotta times, when we
cook, we cook together.

00:01:58.028 --> 00:01:58.861
- I'm not gonna lie.
(Brian laughing)

00:01:58.861 --> 00:02:01.305
He likes to own the
kitchen space, totally!

00:02:01.305 --> 00:02:02.927
- There's some things I
just don't do well, though.

00:02:02.927 --> 00:02:04.994
And she jumps in, and
takes care of all of those.

00:02:04.994 --> 00:02:06.642
- It would be awesome to win a date night.

00:02:06.642 --> 00:02:07.675
We're always working.

00:02:07.675 --> 00:02:10.514
It's not everyday we get to
go out, to a nice restaurant,

00:02:10.514 --> 00:02:11.913
alone, together.
- Right.

00:02:11.913 --> 00:02:13.322
It will force us to go.
(needle scratches)

00:02:13.322 --> 00:02:14.752
- (laughs) Force you?

00:02:14.752 --> 00:02:17.431
- No, it will force us, together, to go.

00:02:17.431 --> 00:02:20.513
- Our second couple have only
been together for one year.

00:02:20.513 --> 00:02:22.980
Please help me welcome, Nico and Felicia!

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.429
(crowd cheering)

00:02:24.429 --> 00:02:26.298
- We cook together, a lot, on Sundays.

00:02:26.298 --> 00:02:28.808
I kinda let him take over,
and I'd, like, drink the wine,

00:02:28.808 --> 00:02:31.876
and say, like, that looks
good, and that looks great!

00:02:31.876 --> 00:02:34.088
I don't cook, but I like to eat! (laughs)

00:02:34.088 --> 00:02:36.419
- And I like to cook, and I'm
Italian, so I have to cook!

00:02:36.419 --> 00:02:37.294
You're nervous.

00:02:37.294 --> 00:02:41.359
- Yeah, I'm nervous about the
knives, and the hot plates.

00:02:41.359 --> 00:02:43.100
I think I'm gonna ruin it for him.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:43.933
- I think we'll do good.

00:02:43.933 --> 00:02:45.433
We're a good team.

00:02:46.546 --> 00:02:48.165
High five!

00:02:48.165 --> 00:02:49.445
- Okay! (laughs)

00:02:49.445 --> 00:02:51.436
- Well, we wish you all the best of luck

00:02:51.436 --> 00:02:52.719
in today's competition.

00:02:52.719 --> 00:02:55.961
Our chef, and judge
for today, Juvia's own,

00:02:55.961 --> 00:02:57.310
Chef Sunny Oh!

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.191
(crowd cheering)

00:02:59.191 --> 00:03:00.372
How are ya doin', Sunny?

00:03:00.372 --> 00:03:02.642
What are our couples
gonna be cooking today?

00:03:02.642 --> 00:03:04.450
- Local, line-caught black grouper.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:08.099
- Let's see if that looks
as good as it sounds!

00:03:08.099 --> 00:03:11.199
(groovy chill music)

00:03:11.199 --> 00:03:12.630
Alright, couples, watch carefully,

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:15.547
because you are going to cook this.

00:03:19.508 --> 00:03:21.091
Yummy, pomegranate.

00:03:24.356 --> 00:03:25.748
- [Sunny] Farro is one
of the oldest grains.

00:03:25.748 --> 00:03:29.831
- [Carl] I think of it as
like, large brown rice.

00:03:35.957 --> 00:03:40.124
Looks like you're gonna
be using that knife a lot!

00:03:54.326 --> 00:03:57.159
(exclaims) Tasty!

00:04:06.465 --> 00:04:07.298
Alright, couples!

00:04:07.298 --> 00:04:09.913
You have 30 minutes, to
cook, and plate this dish!

00:04:09.913 --> 00:04:11.054
Without further ado,

00:04:11.054 --> 00:04:12.964
let's put 30 minutes on the clock, please!

00:04:12.964 --> 00:04:14.297
Let's get tasty!

00:04:15.417 --> 00:04:18.015
(crowd cheering)
(energetic music)

00:04:18.015 --> 00:04:19.682
- No pressure, guys!

00:04:24.905 --> 00:04:25.863
- This is horrible.

00:04:25.863 --> 00:04:27.149
- Spank it, spank it!

00:04:27.149 --> 00:04:27.982
- Thanks, Nico!

00:04:27.982 --> 00:04:28.998
- I gotta bang it, people!

00:04:28.998 --> 00:04:29.831
I gotta bang it!

00:04:29.831 --> 00:04:31.935
I spent ten minutes tryin'
to get pomegranate seeds

00:04:31.935 --> 00:04:33.145
outta the pomegranate.

00:04:33.145 --> 00:04:34.068
- Good job!

00:04:34.068 --> 00:04:35.968
Turn that (expletive) up to ten.

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:36.819
Damn.

00:04:36.819 --> 00:04:40.198
(Fatima groaning)

00:04:40.198 --> 00:04:42.607
- Oh, oh my God!
- Splashdown!

00:04:42.607 --> 00:04:44.047
- You got pomegranate juice all over me.

00:04:44.047 --> 00:04:44.965
- [Felicia] Sorry, baby!

00:04:44.965 --> 00:04:46.754
- I mean, that's, that's
good enough, right?

00:04:46.754 --> 00:04:47.622
- Lunch, brought to you today,

00:04:47.622 --> 00:04:49.004
by the Good Enough Cooking Company!

00:04:49.004 --> 00:04:49.837
- Alright, Sunny.

00:04:49.837 --> 00:04:52.429
So, what is the most
important step to execute,

00:04:52.429 --> 00:04:53.459
in order to win today?

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.800
- I think they need to get
that grouper into the oven

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.060
as quickly as possible.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.208
You know, give it some
color, and then get in,

00:04:58.208 --> 00:05:00.596
because that's probably gonna
take the most amount of time.

00:05:00.596 --> 00:05:01.810
- [Nico] I hope I'm
doing everything right.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:02.886
- [Felicia] Whatever.

00:05:02.886 --> 00:05:03.757
It's too late now.

00:05:03.757 --> 00:05:05.095
- The grade of this
table is a little higher.

00:05:05.095 --> 00:05:07.012
- I know, I'm too tall.

00:05:08.253 --> 00:05:09.704
- [Felicia] Okay, I'm done!

00:05:09.704 --> 00:05:10.537
- [Carl] I'm not gonna lie,

00:05:10.537 --> 00:05:12.543
I didn't know that's how you
get pomegranate seeds out.

00:05:12.543 --> 00:05:14.040
- [Fatima] Yum!

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.460
- It looks great.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:16.293
- [Felicia] Watch it.

00:05:16.293 --> 00:05:17.471
It's gonna burn.

00:05:17.471 --> 00:05:18.533
- Brian, you're good at this.

00:05:18.533 --> 00:05:21.732
- I'm looking at it, and it
looks like you're gonna burn it.

00:05:21.732 --> 00:05:23.432
- [Nico] Am I forgetting something?

00:05:23.432 --> 00:05:26.515
- [Felicia] Put that in the oven now.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.855
- (exclaims) That's a little hot!

00:05:31.855 --> 00:05:32.885
I focused on the fish!

00:05:32.885 --> 00:05:35.804
- Now, the hot stuff.
- Out of the hot stuff!

00:05:35.804 --> 00:05:37.134
- [Brian] Hot, goin' behind.

00:05:37.134 --> 00:05:39.065
Comin' in hot!

00:05:39.065 --> 00:05:40.736
Don't mix 'em up, chef!

00:05:40.736 --> 00:05:42.307
Don't steal my fish!

00:05:42.307 --> 00:05:43.285
- Steal your fish?

00:05:43.285 --> 00:05:44.254
I don't know which one it is!

00:05:44.254 --> 00:05:45.256
- He's doing everything!

00:05:45.256 --> 00:05:46.497
You got this! (laughs)

00:05:46.497 --> 00:05:48.967
- In Japanese technique,
there's the style of cutting,

00:05:48.967 --> 00:05:50.349
it's not just about cutting the product,

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.357
it's how you cut it, the size of it.

00:05:52.357 --> 00:05:53.840
The cucumber, the pomegranate,
the hearts of palm,

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:56.180
wanna remain to be about the same size.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.200
- I hope I don't cut myself.

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:58.867
- [Felicia] You're doing fine.

00:05:58.867 --> 00:06:02.370
(Nico exclaiming)

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:03.607
- Water for our cover.

00:06:03.607 --> 00:06:04.570
- [Fatima] Water for our what?

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:05.403
- [Brian] Cover it.

00:06:05.403 --> 00:06:07.400
I did the fish, made the sauce.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.760
- Alright, it looks like we
are just about to approach

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.290
the 20-minute mark!

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:13.315
- Is there a wrong way to peel this?

00:06:13.315 --> 00:06:15.245
- We need to get this pan
hot enough for the asparagus.

00:06:15.245 --> 00:06:16.920
- Interesting fact about white asparagus,

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.798
is that it's just grown in the dark,

00:06:18.798 --> 00:06:20.249
and that's why it's white.

00:06:20.249 --> 00:06:21.082
- The fish is done.
- Great!

00:06:21.082 --> 00:06:23.037
Can you do the other stuff, too?

00:06:23.037 --> 00:06:24.718
- Look at my thumb!

00:06:24.718 --> 00:06:25.667
(Nico laughing)

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:26.500
- I can't.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.333
- You read it through?

00:06:27.333 --> 00:06:28.314
We're not missin' anything?

00:06:28.314 --> 00:06:29.263
- [Fatima] I don't think so.

00:06:29.263 --> 00:06:31.173
Maybe I should read the directions.

00:06:31.173 --> 00:06:32.461
(Fatima and Brian laughing)

00:06:32.461 --> 00:06:34.403
- Famous last words, read the recipe.

00:06:34.403 --> 00:06:35.994
- [Felicia] If you wouldn't...

00:06:35.994 --> 00:06:37.033
You have to put salt in that.

00:06:37.033 --> 00:06:39.866
I think I, like, diced
everything, pretty nicely.

00:06:39.866 --> 00:06:41.183
- Oh, did you put the timer on?

00:06:41.183 --> 00:06:42.373
- Yeah, that's for the fish.

00:06:42.373 --> 00:06:43.382
- [Felicia] There are things
that you could be doing,

00:06:43.382 --> 00:06:44.689
I'm sure.

00:06:44.689 --> 00:06:45.522
- [Brian] Delicious!

00:06:45.522 --> 00:06:47.066
- (exclaims) Butter!

00:06:47.066 --> 00:06:48.828
- I'm not worried about
just cutting my finger.

00:06:48.828 --> 00:06:51.916
- Brian and Fatima, how are you two doing?

00:06:51.916 --> 00:06:53.797
- I think we're right on track here.

00:06:53.797 --> 00:06:55.257
I think we're gonna put out a nice meal.

00:06:55.257 --> 00:06:56.427
We gotta make the chef proud.

00:06:56.427 --> 00:06:59.158
- Nico and Felicia, how are you two doing?

00:06:59.158 --> 00:06:59.991
- Pretty good, I guess.

00:06:59.991 --> 00:07:01.936
I mean, I'm still alive,
after cutting my thumb.

00:07:01.936 --> 00:07:03.453
- Oh, my, dramatic.

00:07:03.453 --> 00:07:04.791
He's dramatic.

00:07:04.791 --> 00:07:05.642
It is fine.

00:07:05.642 --> 00:07:07.073
- Let's make some noise
for these couples, y'all.

00:07:07.073 --> 00:07:09.543
(crowd cheering)

00:07:09.543 --> 00:07:10.376
- Oh, my God.

00:07:10.376 --> 00:07:11.209
We only have ten minutes!

00:07:11.209 --> 00:07:12.158
(Fatima exclaiming)

00:07:12.158 --> 00:07:13.879
- Did you set it right,
or you set it wrong?

00:07:13.879 --> 00:07:14.712
- No, I did it right.

00:07:14.712 --> 00:07:15.545
- You went this way?

00:07:15.545 --> 00:07:16.968
Is it moving?

00:07:16.968 --> 00:07:18.325
I don't think it's movin'.

00:07:18.325 --> 00:07:19.626
- When I put that on, it went off.

00:07:19.626 --> 00:07:20.459
So, I was just sittin' there,

00:07:20.459 --> 00:07:22.487
and now, I'm like, oh,
oh yeah, turn that on.

00:07:22.487 --> 00:07:23.320
Ready?

00:07:27.217 --> 00:07:29.003
(timer bell ringing)

00:07:29.003 --> 00:07:30.023
- [Felicia] Turn that off.

00:07:30.023 --> 00:07:30.927
- [Nico] I'll be right back!

00:07:30.927 --> 00:07:32.579
- Bye, miss you already.

00:07:32.579 --> 00:07:33.458
- [Fatima] With some flair.

00:07:33.458 --> 00:07:35.291
- I like this, though.

00:07:36.694 --> 00:07:38.067
- It's lookin' pretty good!

00:07:38.067 --> 00:07:40.047
- [Brian] A little bit of pepper on that.

00:07:40.047 --> 00:07:41.086
- No, I didn't.

00:07:41.086 --> 00:07:43.022
- I'm not allowed to do the cooking part.

00:07:43.022 --> 00:07:44.215
- [Nico] No, what am I doing?

00:07:44.215 --> 00:07:45.393
I know!

00:07:45.393 --> 00:07:46.609
- Top it off.

00:07:46.609 --> 00:07:47.442
- [Fatima] I thought it was broken.

00:07:47.442 --> 00:07:48.402
- [Brian] It'll break up.

00:07:48.402 --> 00:07:50.492
- Can you, I can, but I
need you to come back,

00:07:50.492 --> 00:07:52.009
'cause I don't know what to do.

00:07:52.009 --> 00:07:54.873
- That should be a little chewy.

00:07:54.873 --> 00:07:56.828
- Another minute.
- One minute.

00:07:56.828 --> 00:07:58.427
I'm just getting hungry, you know?

00:07:58.427 --> 00:08:00.079
- I only slipped, like,
six times in the kitchen.

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:02.508
- Alright, y'all, two minute warning!

00:08:02.508 --> 00:08:03.341
- We're doing good.

00:08:03.341 --> 00:08:04.931
I think we're almost ready to go!

00:08:04.931 --> 00:08:06.563
- We're outta bowls.

00:08:06.563 --> 00:08:10.230
- We put the farro,
then we put the grouper.

00:08:11.672 --> 00:08:13.139
Isn't the fish, go on top of it?

00:08:13.139 --> 00:08:14.071
- [Brian] The fish leans on one side it,

00:08:14.071 --> 00:08:16.271
and then, the watercress goes in the hole.

00:08:16.271 --> 00:08:18.137
- Seems like a good ratio there.

00:08:18.137 --> 00:08:19.968
- We're gonna make this look sexy.

00:08:19.968 --> 00:08:22.732
(Felicia snickering)

00:08:22.732 --> 00:08:24.333
You put the farro first, and
then we'll put the asparagus,

00:08:24.333 --> 00:08:28.626
kinda lean over like, like
the beautiful video was.

00:08:28.626 --> 00:08:30.132
Looks good with the cress,
make it look real nice.

00:08:30.132 --> 00:08:31.041
- I will.

00:08:31.041 --> 00:08:32.852
- How many asparagus, do we?

00:08:32.852 --> 00:08:33.685
- Yeah.

00:08:33.685 --> 00:08:34.518
- Let's rapido.

00:08:34.518 --> 00:08:35.351
- [Nico] Yeah.

00:08:35.351 --> 00:08:36.184
- [Felicia] Well, put it in there.

00:08:36.184 --> 00:08:38.706
- Oh, I think I put
one too many asparagus.

00:08:38.706 --> 00:08:43.126
- [Carl, Sunny and Crowd]
Ten, nine, eight, seven, six,

00:08:43.126 --> 00:08:45.376
five, four, three, two one!

00:08:47.863 --> 00:08:50.345
- [Carl] Time, time!

00:08:50.345 --> 00:08:53.003
Look at this good
sportsmanship going on here!

00:08:53.003 --> 00:08:55.116
Now, turn to your partner,
and give them a hug!

00:08:55.116 --> 00:08:57.105
That was so intense!

00:08:57.105 --> 00:08:59.044
Aw, I seen that little kiss, Felicia!

00:08:59.044 --> 00:09:01.662
(crowd cheering)

00:09:01.662 --> 00:09:04.329
Up first, we have Brian and Fatima.

00:09:04.329 --> 00:09:05.383
(crowd cheering)

00:09:05.383 --> 00:09:06.732
- There ya go, chef!

00:09:06.732 --> 00:09:07.824
That was a little crazy!

00:09:07.824 --> 00:09:10.433
The 30 minutes goes by a lot
faster than you think it does.

00:09:10.433 --> 00:09:11.475
It was a little stressful.

00:09:11.475 --> 00:09:14.183
I did a lot of dicing, with
all of my fingers still intact.

00:09:14.183 --> 00:09:15.741
